{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794528527896,"sessionID":"ses_e2dc4377affeMLBMP15YBCIej5","part":{"partID":"prt_1d23c3efd0011sMlvhBN0fuUed","sessionID":"ses_e2dc4377affeMLBMP15YBCIej5","messageID":"msg_1d23c3661001A4wkQ06uPL1FLs","type":"tool","id":"call_a87203caa2cd4421938961ff","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/010-reachability-and-attribution/scratch/socket-key.txt"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/010-reachability-and-attribution/scratch/socket-key.txt, lines 1-27\n1: # Socket key: how the daemon socket name is derived\n2: \n3: ## .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/skill-advisor-cli.ts (ADV)\n4: \n5: - `DEFAULT_SOCKET_DIR = '/tmp/system-skill-advisor'` at line 31.\n6: - `ensureSocketEnvironment()` at line 1089 sets `process.env.SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR = DEFAULT_SOCKET_DIR` when it is unset (line 1091). It is called from the tool runner at line 1360.\n7: - `getIpcSocketPath('system-skill-advisor', { dbDir: paths.dbDir })` at line 1363 derives the socket path, through the checkout's own bridge loaded by `loadBridge()` at line 244.\n8: - `paths.dbDir` is `<checkout>/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/database` (line 229), unless `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR` overrides it.\n9: \n10: ## .skilled/bin/system-skill-advisor-launcher.cjs (LCH)\n11: \n12: - `createChildEnv()` at line 312 derives the daemon socket dir at line 336: `filtered.SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR = bridge.resolveIpcSocketDir('system-skill-advisor', { dbDir: resolvedAdvisorDbDir(), env: sourceEnv })`.\n13: - `resolveSessionProxySocketPath()` at line 1058 calls `getIpcSocketPath('system-skill-advisor', { dbDir: resolvedAdvisorDbDir() })` at line 1060.\n14: - `resolvedAdvisorDbDir()` at line 383 resolves to the checkout's `runtime/database`, unless `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR` overrides it.\n15: \n16: ## .skilled/bin/lib/launcher-ipc-bridge.cjs (shared derivation both call)\n17: \n18: - `resolveIpcSocketDir()` at line 139 and `getIpcSocketPath()` at line 162 joins `daemon-ipc.sock`.\n19: - `shouldScopeIpcSocket()` at line 103 returns true for `system-skill-advisor` when the socket dir resolves to `/tmp/system-skill-advisor`, or when `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_SCOPE=database`.\n20: - When scoped, line 152 hashes the canonical database directory with `sha256(dbDir).slice(0, 12)`, and line 153 joins that digest under the socket dir.\n21: - When the derived path exceeds the sun_path limit, `withinLimitOrRelocated()` at line 157 relocates it to `/tmp/system-skill-advisor/<sha256(intended dir).slice(0, 12)>`, still keyed by the intended directory.\n22: \n23: ## Two checkouts\n24: \n25: The scoped digest is taken over the checkout's own database directory, so two checkouts derive two different socket directories and start two daemons. An explicit `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR` other than the default skips that database scope unless `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_SCOPE=database`, so every checkout pointed at that same directory would share one daemon.\n26: \n27: per-checkout","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/010-reachability-and-attribution/scratch/socket-key.txt, lines 1-27\n1: # Socket key: how the daemon socket name is derived\n2: \n3: ## .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/skill-advisor-cli.ts (ADV)\n4: \n5: - `DEFAULT_SOCKET_DIR = '/tmp/system-skill-advisor'` at line 31.\n6: - `ensureSocketEnvironment()` at line 1089 sets `process.env.SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR = DEFAULT_SOCKET_DIR` when it is unset (line 1091). It is called from the tool runner at line 1360.\n7: - `getIpcSocketPath('system-skill-advisor', { dbDir: paths.dbDir })` at line 1363 derives the socket path, through the checkout's own bridge loaded by `loadBridge()` at line 244.\n8: - `paths.dbDir` is `<checkout>/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/database` (line 229), unless `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR` overrides it.\n9: \n10: ## .skilled/bin/system-skill-advisor-launcher.cjs (LCH)\n11: \n12: - `createChildEnv()` at line 312 derives the daemon socket dir at line 336: `filtered.SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR = bridge.resolveIpcSocketDir('system-skill-advisor', { dbDir: resolvedAdvisorDbDir(), env: sourceEnv })`.\n13: - `resolveSessionProxySocketPath()` at line 1058 calls `getIpcSocketPath('system-skill-advisor', { dbDir: resolvedAdvisorDbDir() })` at line 1060.\n14: - `resolvedAdvisorDbDir()` at line 383 resolves to the checkout's `runtime/database`, unless `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR` overrides it.\n15: \n16: ## .skilled/bin/lib/launcher-ipc-bridge.cjs (shared derivation both call)\n17: \n18: - `resolveIpcSocketDir()` at line 139 and `getIpcSocketPath()` at line 162 joins `daemon-ipc.sock`.\n19: - `shouldScopeIpcSocket()` at line 103 returns true for `system-skill-advisor` when the socket dir resolves to `/tmp/system-skill-advisor`, or when `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_SCOPE=database`.\n20: - When scoped, line 152 hashes the canonical database directory with `sha256(dbDir).slice(0, 12)`, and line 153 joins that digest under the socket dir.\n21: - When the derived path exceeds the sun_path limit, `withinLimitOrRelocated()` at line 157 relocates it to `/tmp/system-skill-advisor/<sha256(intended dir).slice(0, 12)>`, still keyed by the intended directory.\n22: \n23: ## Two checkouts\n24: \n25: The scoped digest is taken over the checkout's own database directory, so two checkouts derive two different socket directories and start two daemons. An explicit `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR` other than the default skips that database scope unless `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_SCOPE=database`, so every checkout pointed at that same directory would share one daemon.\n26: \n27: per-checkout"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/010-reachability-and-attribution/scratch/socket-key.txt\"}"},"time":{"start":1794528526077,"end":1794528527896}}}}
