{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794528582802,"sessionID":"ses_e2dc4377affeMLBMP15YBCIej5","part":{"partID":"prt_1d23d175d001N7kItSc9DCNnPg","sessionID":"ses_e2dc4377affeMLBMP15YBCIej5","messageID":"msg_1d23cf6f7001cWqt4J6NIie4TT","type":"tool","id":"call_f2edf10a8adf44149c8fa867","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":60,"offset":255,"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/010-reachability-and-attribution/spec.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/010-reachability-and-attribution/spec.md, lines 255-314\n255: \n256: ### Security\n257: - **NFR-S01**: The two check scripts and the backfill write no file in the home folder. The Codex check reads one config file and prints no hash value.\n258: - **NFR-S02**: No task reads or prints holdout prompt text. The backfill refuses a holdout row id through the runner's own lookup.\n259: \n260: ### Reliability\n261: - **NFR-R01**: A replay that times out or prints no head yields null offer fields with an `offerError` code, never a crash.\n262: \n263: ---\n264: \n265: <!-- ANCHOR:edge-cases -->\n266: ## L2: EDGE CASES\n267: \n268: - Empty input: a run log with no lines makes the backfill write an empty file and exit 0.\n269: - Maximum input: an ambiguous head that names two commands records the first one.\n270: - Failure path: a line with no `locator.projectDir` gets null offer fields and `offerError: 'no_checkout'`, and the rest of the log is still written.\n271: <!-- /ANCHOR:edge-cases -->\n272: \n273: ---\n274: \n275: <!-- ANCHOR:complexity -->\n276: ## L2: COMPLEXITY ASSESSMENT\n277: \n278: | Dimension | Score | Notes |\n279: |-----------|-------|-------|\n280: | Scope | 15/25 | About 18 files and 900 lines across the harness, two doctor scripts, the DSH bundle and the install guide |\n281: | Risk | 10/25 | No scoring or brief change, and a measurement output that changes meaning |\n282: | Research | 6/20 | The research names each change, and the code read is done |\n283: | **Total** | **31/70** | **Level 2** |\n284: <!-- /ANCHOR:complexity -->\n285: \n286: ---\n287: \n288: <!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n289: ## 10. OPEN QUESTIONS\n290: \n291: ### Resolved\n292: \n293: Each answer below is an autonomous decision under the packet goal's D1 (\"Run autonomously and ask the operator nothing. Take the recommended option\"), recorded on 2026-11-13.\n294: \n295: - How is the offer decided? Decision: replay the Claude prompt hook inside the run's checkout and read the first line of its brief (Recommended). The renderer is shared by every runtime today, so one replay stands for all six, and the head is what the model saw. Reading the recommendation JSON instead would count a hub's attached command that the pre-005 head never printed.\n296: - When does the replay run? Decision: after the turn and its restore (Recommended), so the replay cannot warm the daemon for the turn it describes or add a changed path to it.\n297: - How is `briefDelivered` decided? Decision: `true` or `false` only where the stored session shows the brief (Claude's raw transcript and Pi's records), and `\"unknown\"` for Codex, Devin, OpenCode and DSH (Recommended). Codex joins the decided set only after T031 shows a delivered brief in a rollout (T032).\n298: - Which checkout does the backfill ask? Decision: each line's own `locator.projectDir` (Recommended). The before arm's lines already name their arena, so no extra flag is needed.\n299: - What counts as \"offered\" in the summary? Decision: the line's `offeredCommand` names the row's expected command by namespace and name (Recommended).\n300: - What is the size of the set for `arm incomplete`? Decision: the largest run count of any runtime in the same arm (Recommended). The scorer cannot import the runner's sets, and a new flag would duplicate them.\n301: - What does `wrote` mean? Decision: the run line lists at least one changed path (Recommended). The runner observed it in git, which is stronger than a transcript event.\n302: - Where does the Codex check run? Decision: a new script called from `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` (Recommended), the route the research names and the one that already reads `~/.codex/hooks.json`.\n303: - Is the DSH default change still worth building after the refutation? Decision: yes, as asked (Recommended), with the gain stated as small. Only a patch that omits the flag benefits, and the arm does not change.\n304: - The workflow's step 5 explorer agents, its `research/research.md` output and its step 6 continuity save. Decision: skipped (Recommended). The claims were read in code directly, the research exists in phase 009 and the spec authoring card forbids `generate-context.js` in a planning worker.\n305: - The level helper. Decision: Level 2 as the brief states (Recommended).\n306: - `implementation-summary.md`. Decision: not scaffolded now (Recommended). It is written by the last task, as the card says.\n307: \n308: ### Open\n309: \n310: None.\n311: <!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n312: \n313: ---\n314: \n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 315]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/010-reachability-and-attribution/spec.md, lines 255-314\n255: \n256: ### Security\n257: - **NFR-S01**: The two check scripts and the backfill write no file in the home folder. The Codex check reads one config file and prints no hash value.\n258: - **NFR-S02**: No task reads or prints holdout prompt text. The backfill refuses a holdout row id through the runner's own lookup.\n259: \n260: ### Reliability\n261: - **NFR-R01**: A replay that times out or prints no head yields null offer fields with an `offerError` code, never a crash.\n262: \n263: ---\n264: \n265: <!-- ANCHOR:edge-cases -->\n266: ## L2: EDGE CASES\n267: \n268: - Empty input: a run log with no lines makes the backfill write an empty file and exit 0.\n269: - Maximum input: an ambiguous head that names two commands records the first one.\n270: - Failure path: a line with no `locator.projectDir` gets null offer fields and `offerError: 'no_checkout'`, and the rest of the log is still written.\n271: <!-- /ANCHOR:edge-cases -->\n272: \n273: ---\n274: \n275: <!-- ANCHOR:complexity -->\n276: ## L2: COMPLEXITY ASSESSMENT\n277: \n278: | Dimension | Score | Notes |\n279: |-----------|-------|-------|\n280: | Scope | 15/25 | About 18 files and 900 lines across the harness, two doctor scripts, the DSH bundle and the install guide |\n281: | Risk | 10/25 | No scoring or brief change, and a measurement output that changes meaning |\n282: | Research | 6/20 | The research names each change, and the code read is done |\n283: | **Total** | **31/70** | **Level 2** |\n284: <!-- /ANCHOR:complexity -->\n285: \n286: ---\n287: \n288: <!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n289: ## 10. OPEN QUESTIONS\n290: \n291: ### Resolved\n292: \n293: Each answer below is an autonomous decision under the packet goal's D1 (\"Run autonomously and ask the operator nothing. Take the recommended option\"), recorded on 2026-11-13.\n294: \n295: - How is the offer decided? Decision: replay the Claude prompt hook inside the run's checkout and read the first line of its brief (Recommended). The renderer is shared by every runtime today, so one replay stands for all six, and the head is what the model saw. Reading the recommendation JSON instead would count a hub's attached command that the pre-005 head never printed.\n296: - When does the replay run? Decision: after the turn and its restore (Recommended), so the replay cannot warm the daemon for the turn it describes or add a changed path to it.\n297: - How is `briefDelivered` decided? Decision: `true` or `false` only where the stored session shows the brief (Claude's raw transcript and Pi's records), and `\"unknown\"` for Codex, Devin, OpenCode and DSH (Recommended). Codex joins the decided set only after T031 shows a delivered brief in a rollout (T032).\n298: - Which checkout does the backfill ask? Decision: each line's own `locator.projectDir` (Recommended). The before arm's lines already name their arena, so no extra flag is needed.\n299: - What counts as \"offered\" in the summary? Decision: the line's `offeredCommand` names the row's expected command by namespace and name (Recommended).\n300: - What is the size of the set for `arm incomplete`? Decision: the largest run count of any runtime in the same arm (Recommended). The scorer cannot import the runner's sets, and a new flag would duplicate them.\n301: - What does `wrote` mean? Decision: the run line lists at least one changed path (Recommended). The runner observed it in git, which is stronger than a transcript event.\n302: - Where does the Codex check run? Decision: a new script called from `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` (Recommended), the route the research names and the one that already reads `~/.codex/hooks.json`.\n303: - Is the DSH default change still worth building after the refutation? Decision: yes, as asked (Recommended), with the gain stated as small. Only a patch that omits the flag benefits, and the arm does not change.\n304: - The workflow's step 5 explorer agents, its `research/research.md` output and its step 6 continuity save. Decision: skipped (Recommended). The claims were read in code directly, the research exists in phase 009 and the spec authoring card forbids `generate-context.js` in a planning worker.\n305: - The level helper. Decision: Level 2 as the brief states (Recommended).\n306: - `implementation-summary.md`. Decision: not scaffolded now (Recommended). It is written by the last task, as the card says.\n307: \n308: ### Open\n309: \n310: None.\n311: <!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n312: \n313: ---\n314: \n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 315]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\":60,\"offset\":255,\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/010-reachability-and-attribution/spec.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794528581469,"end":1794528582802}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794528582810,"sessionID":"ses_e2dc4377affeMLBMP15YBCIej5","part":{"partID":"prt_1d23d19d6001BINeidaS2EOEK7","sessionID":"ses_e2dc4377affeMLBMP15YBCIej5","messageID":"msg_1d23cf6f7001cWqt4J6NIie4TT","type":"tool","id":"call_3fbf5a4a7aba41babc1d2bf8","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"sed -n 1,60p .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/vitest.config.ts 2>/dev/null || ls .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime | head -30","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// MODULE: System Skill Advisor Vitest Config\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nimport path from 'node:path';\n\nconst TEST_TIMEOUT_MS = 30_000;\nconst TEARDOWN_TIMEOUT_MS = 1_000;\nconst INCLUDE_BENCHES = process.env.SPECKIT_RUN_BENCHES === 'true';\n// The stress suites are excluded from the default run because they are slow, not\n// because they are unwanted. Without a way to opt in they were unreachable: no\n// script and no pattern selected them, so 21 files sat in the tree running never.\n// Opting in REPLACES the default set rather than adding to it: these suites churn\n// the daemon, its socket and its lease, and running them beside the ordinary\n// suites fails a handful of those on shared state rather than on their own logic.\nconst INCLUDE_STRESS = process.env.SPECKIT_RUN_STRESS === 'true';\n\n// A plain object export instead of vitest's defineConfig wrapper: the config is\n// loaded by node's own module graph, where a bare `vitest` import resolves to\n// whatever node_modules sits next to this file. CI's routing job runs the suites\n// under a vitest pinned through npx, which can differ from the runtime's own\n// vitest range, so importing from the package here could load a second vitest\n// copy. defineConfig is an identity type-helper; dropping it changes nothing at\n// runtime.\nexport default ({\n  root: import.meta.dirname,\n  test: {\n    include: [\n      ...(INCLUDE_STRESS ? ['stress-test/**/*.vitest.ts'] : ['tests/**/*.vitest.ts']),\n      ...(INCLUDE_BENCHES ? ['bench/**/*.bench.ts'] : []),\n    ],\n    exclude: [\n      'node_modules',\n      'dist',\n      ...(INCLUDE_BENCHES ? [] : ['bench/**/*.bench.ts']),\n    ],\n    setupFiles: [\n      path.resolve(import.meta.dirname, '../../system-spec-kit/runtime/tests/_support/vitest-setup.ts'),\n    ],\n    fileParallelism: false,\n    globals: true,\n    environment: 'node',\n    testTimeout: TEST_TIMEOUT_MS,\n    teardownTimeout: TEARDOWN_TIMEOUT_MS,\n    alias: {\n      '@lib': path.resolve(import.meta.dirname, 'lib'),\n    },\n  },\n});\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// MODULE: System Skill Advisor Vitest Config\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nimport path from 'node:path';\n\nconst TEST_TIMEOUT_MS = 30_000;\nconst TEARDOWN_TIMEOUT_MS = 1_000;\nconst INCLUDE_BENCHES = process.env.SPECKIT_RUN_BENCHES === 'true';\n// The stress suites are excluded from the default run because they are slow, not\n// because they are unwanted. Without a way to opt in they were unreachable: no\n// script and no pattern selected them, so 21 files sat in the tree running never.\n// Opting in REPLACES the default set rather than adding to it: these suites churn\n// the daemon, its socket and its lease, and running them beside the ordinary\n// suites fails a handful of those on shared state rather than on their own logic.\nconst INCLUDE_STRESS = process.env.SPECKIT_RUN_STRESS === 'true';\n\n// A plain object export instead of vitest's defineConfig wrapper: the config is\n// loaded by node's own module graph, where a bare `vitest` import resolves to\n// whatever node_modules sits next to this file. CI's routing job runs the suites\n// under a vitest pinned through npx, which can differ from the runtime's own\n// vitest range, so importing from the package here could load a second vitest\n// copy. defineConfig is an identity type-helper; dropping it changes nothing at\n// runtime.\nexport default ({\n  root: import.meta.dirname,\n  test: {\n    include: [\n      ...(INCLUDE_STRESS ? ['stress-test/**/*.vitest.ts'] : ['tests/**/*.vitest.ts']),\n      ...(INCLUDE_BENCHES ? ['bench/**/*.bench.ts'] : []),\n    ],\n    exclude: [\n      'node_modules',\n      'dist',\n      ...(INCLUDE_BENCHES ? [] : ['bench/**/*.bench.ts']),\n    ],\n    setupFiles: [\n      path.resolve(import.meta.dirname, '../../system-spec-kit/runtime/tests/_support/vitest-setup.ts'),\n    ],\n    fileParallelism: false,\n    globals: true,\n    environment: 'node',\n    testTimeout: TEST_TIMEOUT_MS,\n    teardownTimeout: TEARDOWN_TIMEOUT_MS,\n    alias: {\n      '@lib': path.resolve(import.meta.dirname, 'lib'),\n    },\n  },\n});\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"sed -n 1,60p .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/vitest.config.ts 2>/dev/null || ls .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime | head -30\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794528582102,"end":1794528582810}}}}
